1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:02,460
Here's the bag.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:03,870
Will he be OK, Dad?

3
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:09,780
I hope so.

4
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:11,070
That's it.

5
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,560
That's the way.

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:15,800
That's it. There.

7
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,870
Oh, it's going to be all right.

8
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:20,140
That's it.

9
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,170
Wrap him in the blanket, Dad!

10
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,080
That's it. That's it.

11
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,010
It's all right, Albert.

12
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:28,700
You're going to be OK.

13
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,100
I want my daddy!

14
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,740
We'll take you to him.

15
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:39,210
Easy now. Easy does it. That's it.

16
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:41,010
Your dad is quite a guy.

17
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:43,000
I know, Grandpa.

18
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,660
How is he, Philip?

19
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:45,770
He's asleep.

20
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:47,240
He's going to be fine.

21
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,620
How can I thank all of you?

22
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:50,090
Thank my son Robbie.

23
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,380
He pulled him out of the water.

24
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:52,730
I'm very grateful, Robbie.

25
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,600
Dad saved him, not me.

26
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,220
I'm so thankful to all of you.

27
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:00,750
So long.

28
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:02,870
He's a lucky boy.

29
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:05,710
Well, what do you say we get back to our fishing?

30
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,420
That's a great idea.

31
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:13,140
Uh-oh. It's probably the hospital.

32
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,980
I have to get to a phone.

33
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,140
It probably means we can't stay.

34
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:24,990
That's OK.

35
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:27,150
One of my patients has a high fever,

36
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:29,920
and I have to go to the hospital.

37
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:30,750
I'm sorry, Robbie.

38
00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:33,340
I guess I ruined your day.

39
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:39,990
You didn't ruin my day, Dad.

40
00:01:39,990 --> 00:02:08,570
I understand. I really do.

41
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:10,270
Why are you back so early?

42
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:12,150
Philip had to go back to the hospital.

43
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:13,820
He had an emergency.

44
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,850
Oh, that's too bad, Robbie.

45
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:17,040
Did it spoil your fun?

46
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,750
No, Mom. We had a great time.

47
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:21,990
Well, did you do any fishing?

48
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:28,390
Yeah, we caught lots of them. Look!

49
00:02:28,390 --> 00:02:31,950
They had a special on frozen fish down at the supermarket.

50
00:02:31,950 --> 00:02:35,470
Oh, you really had a bad day.

51
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:37,270
We had a good day.

52
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:40,150
Robbie pulled a boy out of the water.

53
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:42,720
And Dad saved his life.

54
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,370
He's a terrific doctor, Mom.

55
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:58,580
I know.

56
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:00,630
Hi, Pop. Hi, Son.

57
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:02,840
Hello, Dad.

58
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,560
What a day!

59
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,540
How about a cup of coffee, Son?

60
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:15,780
I'd love a cup of coffee.

61
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,290
How was the patient?

62
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:19,410
She'll be fine.

63
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:21,680
Was it serious?

64
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,500
No.

65
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,400
Until today, I was never really interested in medicine.

66
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:31,040
Well, it's hard work.

67
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:33,520
Now I know.

68
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,760
I had a good time today, Robbie.

69
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,130
Me, too.

70
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:41,170
Why don't we do it again?

71
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:43,780
Can we? When?

72
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:45,960
How about next Saturday?

73
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:48,340
Won't you be busy?

74
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:51,440
I'm changing my schedule.

75
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,320
Well, do we have a date?

76
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,500
We sure do, Dad.

77
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:57,630
Grandpa, can you come?

78
00:03:57,630 --> 00:04:00,530
I have other plans, Robbie.

79
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:04,700
But I think you two can have a good time together without me.

80
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:07,700
No, Dad, and certainly not without the right magic.
